Your task is to:
Calculate the total data usage for the week Calculate the average daily usage Count the number of days where usage exceeded the average
Finally, print:
Total usage Average usage (integer division) Number of days with usage greater than average
Input Format
A single line containing 7 space-separated integers representing data usage (in MB) for each day
Constraints
0 ≤ usage ≤ 10^4 Exactly 7 integers will be provided Output average should be integer division
Output Format
Print three values separated by space:
total_usage average_usage count_above_average
Sample Input 0
100 200 300 400 500 600 700
Sample Output 0
2800 400 3
Sample Input 1
10 20 30 40 50 60 70
Sample Output 1
280 40 3

//code
#include<stdio.h>
int main(){
int arr[7];
int total =0;
for(int i=0;i<7;i++){
    scanf("%d",&arr[i]);
   total +=arr[i];
}
int avg=total/7;
int count =0;
for(int i=0;i<7;i++){
    if(arr[i]>avg){
        count++;
    }
}
printf("%d %d %d",total ,avg ,count);
return 0;
}

